      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A historic toll station operated by Ben Pitts, later expanded by the Tillitt family, once served travelers heading into the San Bernardino Mountains.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.digital-desert.wrightwoodcalifornia.com/green-valley-lake/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The 1915 Trading Post and gas station beside the tollhouse marked the early commercial hub of Green Valley Lake.",
